{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed as change 2307, patch set 2.\n\nImportant property of this CI setup, discovered here: the Verified lane takes the workflow DEFINITION from trusted main and only the TREE from the patchset (the 'classify Verify route from trusted main' step). A NEWLY ADDED job therefore cannot run on its own change — the sandbox-enforcement job did not appear in the run at all. Verified +1 on this change proves the parity fixes; it does NOT prove the lane. The lane first executes post-merge.\n\nSo I verified the lane end-to-end locally instead, running its exact container command against a clean 'git archive HEAD' export:\n\n  docker run --privileged -e REBAR_REQUIRE_SANDBOX_ENFORCEMENT=1 python:3.13-slim\n    -> pip install .[dev]; pytest tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py\n  RESULT: 43 passed, 0 skipped\n\n0 skipped is the load-bearing number: with the flag set, the @live enforcement tests RAN under a real bwrap on Linux rather than skipping. That is exactly what the lane does.\n\nPatch set 1 failed CI on three repo-policy guards, all legitimate: the job set is pinned to {lint, pip-audit, test}, the pytest lane set was counted, and any step running a repo file must skip cleanly when a base predates it. All three now updated to admit the new job without weakening their intent. One fix touched the tree-skew detector: its regex 'scripts/[...].py' was unanchored, so it read tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py as the gate script scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py — a path that does not exist and that no if-present guard could satisfy. Added a path-boundary lookbehind, and kept my own if-present guard regardless since the skew risk is real.\n\nThose guards live in tests/unit/, which my narrower pre-push selection did not cover — that is why they reached CI. Now running tests/unit + tests/scripts in parallel before pushing: 15337 passed, 0 failed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787891429571539001,"uuid":"8fc3c305-5c22-46f9-877f-212183d4a694"}